WEBVTT

1
01:01:39.810 --> 01:02:06.810
Have new agreements been made with the Lord?

2
01:02:10.810 --> 01:02:27.810
God is a person. Jesus is a person. You can talk to him.

3
01:02:27.810 --> 01:02:31.810
It is so important that you make an appointment with him. That you talk to him.

4
01:02:31.810 --> 01:02:37.810
That says, here I am again in 2026. I want to come to you. I want to be more with you. I want to draw closer to you.

5
01:02:37.810 --> 01:02:44.810
So Lord, I want to ask you to bless the people in Open Church through your Holy Spirit.

6
01:02:44.810 --> 01:02:51.810
Here that we will draw closer to you. And the Holy Spirit is the third person of the Trinity.

7
01:02:51.810 --> 01:03:00.810
And it is his task to defend you as an advocate. But it is also his task to reveal the Son and the Father in you.

8
01:03:00.810 --> 01:03:11.810
This is what He does. And Holy Spirit, I want to ask you to give everyone in Open Church a new, new revelation of the glory of King Jesus.

9
01:03:11.810 --> 01:03:15.810
And we pray this together in the name of Jesus. Amen. Amen.

10
01:03:15.810 --> 01:03:19.810
Amen. Please take a seat. But give someone a high five or a hug first.

11
01:03:19.810 --> 01:03:24.810
Quickly say hello and then we will begin.

12
01:03:24.810 --> 01:03:26.810
Much to discuss.

13
01:03:35.810 --> 01:03:37.810
Hallelujah.

14
01:03:39.810 --> 01:03:43.810
Quickly say hello and then sit down.

15
01:03:43.810 --> 01:03:49.810
Because I have mucho, mucho to discuss. Hallelujah.

16
01:03:55.810 --> 01:04:03.810
I brought my notebook from my personal devotion today.

17
01:04:03.810 --> 01:04:12.810
And it looks different when you talk to God in your personal time than a structured sermon.

18
01:04:12.810 --> 01:04:18.810
What am I saying anyway? I don't write anything for sermons anyway, but whatever.

19
01:04:18.810 --> 01:04:24.810
When you are talking to God himself, then Scripture resonates within you.

20
01:04:24.810 --> 01:04:31.810
When you read something in Scripture, it resonates in your life.

21
01:04:31.810 --> 01:04:37.810
You experience things, and at the moment you experience it and then read something in Scripture,

22
01:04:37.810 --> 01:04:44.810
then resonance, to resonate means it starts to vibrate along, it starts to move along.

23
01:04:44.810 --> 01:04:51.810
And then you read the Bible and wow, this speaks to me now.

24
01:04:51.810 --> 01:04:58.810
These are real situations, the Bible is written by real people driven by the Holy Spirit.

25
01:04:58.810 --> 01:05:00.810
This is how Scripture is put together.

26
01:05:00.810 --> 01:05:06.810
Every Scripture is God-breathed, says the Bible, written by human hands.

27
01:05:06.810 --> 01:05:13.810
Except for the Ten Commandments, which were written with God's finger. Hallelujah.

28
01:05:13.810 --> 01:05:23.810
And when you have intimacy with God and you go through things and then read certain points.

29
01:05:23.810 --> 01:05:29.810
In my situation, I read the Bible using the SOAP method.

30
01:05:29.810 --> 01:05:35.810
The SOAP method is that I have to read something every day.

31
01:05:35.810 --> 01:05:41.810
On Monday I read this, and the next Monday I read the next chapter of that book.

32
01:05:41.810 --> 01:05:48.810
On Tuesday I read a different book, and the next Tuesday I read the next chapter of that book from the previous Tuesday.

33
01:05:48.810 --> 01:05:53.810
And so you go, Old Testament, New Testament, Old Testament, New Testament, this is how you go through the Bible.

34
01:05:53.810 --> 01:05:57.810
And the SOAP methodology is Scripture, Observation, Application, Prayer.

35
01:05:57.810 --> 01:06:05.810
So I write a big S for which verse from that chapter spoke to me the most.

36
01:06:05.810 --> 01:06:09.810
Below that an O, Observation, what do I think this says?

37
01:06:09.810 --> 01:06:13.810
How does it resonate? What do I think it means?

38
01:06:13.810 --> 01:06:21.810
The Application, the A, is what can I do with it? How does this speak into my life? How am I going to put this into action?

39
01:06:21.810 --> 01:06:26.810
And the P is the Prayer. Always when you read the Bible, pray as well.

40
01:06:26.810 --> 01:06:30.810
That the Lord can apply it or that I can apply it through the Holy Spirit.

41
01:06:30.810 --> 01:06:35.810
You need the Lord to live out the Bible. Hallelujah.

42
01:06:35.810 --> 01:06:42.810
And the past time has been an exciting time, I can tell you.

43
01:06:42.810 --> 01:06:46.810
Last week was a rollercoaster week.

44
01:06:46.810 --> 01:06:52.810
And last week my son got sick and we had to go to the hospital.

45
01:06:52.810 --> 01:06:58.810
And that was crazy, because I want to be in the church and I don't want to see my son cry.

46
01:06:58.810 --> 01:07:02.810
And so it was really a rollercoaster, so that was very strange.

47
01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:09.810
And we just came out of the hospital. Actually, the hospital said we had to stay a few more days than my impatience allowed.

48
01:07:09.810 --> 01:07:15.810
And so I was there heavily frustrated, I want to get out of this hospital.

49
01:07:15.810 --> 01:07:20.810
Despite a lot of respect for people who do such services.

50
01:07:20.810 --> 01:07:23.810
What a nice hospital, what lovely people.

51
01:07:23.810 --> 01:07:25.810
Praise the Lord, pray for him.

52
01:07:25.810 --> 01:07:35.810
And I come out of the hospital on Tuesday and on Wednesday we had a wonderful wedding of Danny and Kezaja.

53
01:07:35.810 --> 01:07:37.810
I believe you are here too, right Danny and Kezaja?

54
01:07:40.810 --> 01:07:47.810
Danny, Kezaja, I think your wedding was one of the best weddings I have ever had.

55
01:07:47.810 --> 01:07:51.810
I love all weddings, because Jesus is there.

56
01:07:51.810 --> 01:07:59.810
But you know what, I love weddings where Christians come together and wrestle with the King.

57
01:07:59.810 --> 01:08:04.810
That is not stiff, that is just wrestling.

58
01:08:05.810 --> 01:08:10.810
And last Wednesday it was a worship wedding ceremony.

59
01:08:10.810 --> 01:08:11.810
How nice is that?

60
01:08:11.810 --> 01:08:18.810
That you unanimously also desire that that couple be blessed in the marvelous name of Jesus.

61
01:08:18.810 --> 01:08:24.810
So then I'm going from the hospital a bit to a wedding.

62
01:08:28.810 --> 01:08:32.810
And then Thursday came, and Thursday was, wow.

63
01:08:33.810 --> 01:08:36.810
Okay, what do I want to discuss with you?

64
01:08:37.810 --> 01:08:43.810
Before the turn of the year, regarding the new construction project,

65
01:08:43.810 --> 01:08:51.810
we laid down a fleece here and shared the story of Gideon,

66
01:08:51.810 --> 01:08:54.810
who asks for a confirmation from the Lord.

67
01:08:55.810 --> 01:09:00.810
Gideon says to the Lord, if I must go into battle against the enemy,

68
01:09:00.810 --> 01:09:05.810
it's not just about what the goal was,

69
01:09:05.810 --> 01:09:08.810
but it's about, if this is your will, says Gideon,

70
01:09:08.810 --> 01:09:14.810
then I want to ask you if this fleece, and then he lays out a fleece, a test,

71
01:09:14.810 --> 01:09:19.810
and then he says, Lord, if it is your will that I do this,

72
01:09:19.810 --> 01:09:21.810
then I want to ask you for a confirmation,

73
01:09:21.810 --> 01:09:27.810
and then tomorrow that fleece must be wet and the ground,

74
01:09:27.810 --> 01:09:33.810
there will be no morning dew on the ground, the ground will be dry and the fleece will be wet.

75
01:09:34.810 --> 01:09:41.810
And so said, so done, you can always ask the Lord for confirmations, church.

76
01:09:41.810 --> 01:09:45.810
The Bible says, do not test the Lord, that is something else.

77
01:09:45.810 --> 01:09:50.810
So you must not challenge God, like, Lord, I'm going to jump off this roof,

78
01:09:50.810 --> 01:09:54.810
and you must protect me then, that is literally what Satan asks Jesus.

79
01:09:54.810 --> 01:09:56.810
Like, jump off the roof, see how it goes.

80
01:09:56.810 --> 01:09:59.810
And Jesus says, no, that is testing the Lord.

81
01:09:59.810 --> 01:10:06.810
You may ask the Lord for confirmations, and be specific when you ask for confirmations.

82
01:10:06.810 --> 01:10:08.810
Always be specific.

83
01:10:08.810 --> 01:10:13.810
Ask Him specific questions, those are also bold prayers,

84
01:10:13.810 --> 01:10:16.810
I have done this several times in my life,

85
01:10:16.810 --> 01:10:21.810
that I really boldly said, Lord, by then I want to see that happen,

86
01:10:21.810 --> 01:10:23.810
otherwise I just know that it is not Your will.

87
01:10:23.810 --> 01:10:25.810
And believe me, I am not going to list them all now,

88
01:10:25.810 --> 01:10:28.810
but those are sometimes very bold prayers.

89
01:10:28.810 --> 01:10:32.810
Because then it comes down to it, then it really comes down to it, it's either yes or no.

90
01:10:32.810 --> 01:10:34.810
Do you understand what I mean?

91
01:10:34.810 --> 01:10:43.810
And we did that as well with the building project on one of the last Sundays of the year.

92
01:10:43.810 --> 01:10:48.810
I can look back for a moment, that was on the Sunday of the week,

93
01:10:48.810 --> 01:10:52.810
Sunday, December 21, I think.

94
01:10:54.810 --> 01:10:59.810
Yes, that was Sunday, December 21, because here I am looking at it.

95
01:11:01.810 --> 01:11:07.810
Because we are, as a church, one hundred percent convinced

96
01:11:07.810 --> 01:11:12.810
that the Lord has given us a revelation that we need to build.

97
01:11:12.810 --> 01:11:15.810
You see, people are sitting in the back on wooden benches,

98
01:11:15.810 --> 01:11:18.810
people are sitting in the overflow of the bar area,

99
01:11:18.810 --> 01:11:20.810
the church is filling up,

100
01:11:20.810 --> 01:11:23.810
and it's not just a filled church that is so beautiful,

101
01:11:23.810 --> 01:11:27.810
it is that you may bless people in the name of Jesus in marriage.

102
01:11:27.810 --> 01:11:30.810
It is wonderful that you may baptize people in the name of Jesus.

103
01:11:30.810 --> 01:11:34.810
It is wonderful that you may guide teenagers between 12 and 18,

104
01:11:34.810 --> 01:11:38.810
so that they stay out of the world and may remain in God's kingdom

105
01:11:38.810 --> 01:11:41.810
during those crucial years of their lives.

106
01:11:41.810 --> 01:11:44.810
What an important task, which we should not trivialize,

107
01:11:44.810 --> 01:11:46.810
of yes, it's just the youth.

108
01:11:46.810 --> 01:11:49.810
There is a world of difference between 12 and 18,

109
01:11:49.810 --> 01:11:52.810
whether you go with Jesus or do not go with Jesus.

110
01:11:52.810 --> 01:11:54.810
That is by the way also true for adults,

111
01:11:54.810 --> 01:11:57.810
but the whole world pulls so hard at those teenagers.

112
01:11:57.810 --> 01:12:03.810
And so, there is no success to be seen in the number of seats filled in the church.

113
01:12:03.810 --> 01:12:06.810
The church's success, let me put it better,

114
01:12:06.810 --> 01:12:11.810
the fruit of the church is to be measured by discipleship.

115
01:12:11.810 --> 01:12:13.810
That is what it should be measured against.

116
01:12:13.810 --> 01:12:16.810
People who are going for a new start, people who are going to read their Bible,

117
01:12:16.810 --> 01:12:18.810
people who stop sinning,

118
01:12:18.810 --> 01:12:20.810
people who get baptized in the name of Jesus,

119
01:12:20.810 --> 01:12:22.810
and do not stay home the following week,

120
01:12:22.810 --> 01:12:27.810
because they got baptized once due to the hype of social media, christianity,

121
01:12:27.810 --> 01:12:31.810
but that they simply get baptized and that they keep coming to the Lord.

122
01:12:31.810 --> 01:12:33.810
That is what the Lord is looking for.

123
01:12:33.810 --> 01:12:36.810
And I see that Open Church is bearing fruit,

124
01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:38.810
and I am happy with Open Church.

125
01:12:38.810 --> 01:12:42.810
And just like Paul wants to say to the Philippian church, I also want to say to Open Church,

126
01:12:42.810 --> 01:12:44.810
we are doing well, people.

127
01:12:44.810 --> 01:12:48.810
Yes, there are always fires to put out,

128
01:12:48.810 --> 01:12:50.810
yes, there is sin to forgive,

129
01:12:50.810 --> 01:12:52.810
yes, there are things to restore,

130
01:12:52.810 --> 01:12:55.810
but I see that there is a growth of fruit in Open Church,

131
01:12:55.810 --> 01:12:56.810
and I am happy about it,

132
01:12:56.810 --> 01:13:00.810
and I say in Open Church in 2026 that we will continue with that,

133
01:13:00.810 --> 01:13:02.810
and that is why we need to build,

134
01:13:02.810 --> 01:13:05.810
and that is why God has given us a revelation in 2023,

135
01:13:05.810 --> 01:13:08.810
it is time to start building.

136
01:13:08.810 --> 01:13:11.810
And from the moment we knew we had to start building,

137
01:13:11.810 --> 01:13:13.810
I asked the Lord,

138
01:13:13.810 --> 01:13:16.810
please give a green light,

139
01:13:16.810 --> 01:13:18.810
please give confirmations?

140
01:13:18.810 --> 01:13:21.810
And the Lord gave supernatural confirmations.

141
01:13:21.810 --> 01:13:23.810
by giving two pieces of land,

142
01:13:23.810 --> 01:13:26.810
yes, I repeat things so you can remember them well,

143
01:13:26.810 --> 01:13:29.810
by giving two pieces of land, which is supernatural,

144
01:13:29.810 --> 01:13:31.810
never occurs in the world.

145
01:13:31.810 --> 01:13:34.810
We have received permits which is favor with God and people,

146
01:13:34.810 --> 01:13:36.810
as the Bible says,

147
01:13:36.810 --> 01:13:39.810
and the permits are never granted so easily nowadays.

148
01:13:40.810 --> 01:13:43.810
There is always trouble and distress, there are always lawsuits,

149
01:13:43.810 --> 01:13:46.810
there are always delays in applying for permits,

150
01:13:46.810 --> 01:13:50.810
but Open Church stands in favor with God and the government,

151
01:13:50.810 --> 01:13:52.810
and that is what King Jesus is praised for,

152
01:13:52.810 --> 01:13:55.810
because we received our permit immediately.

153
01:13:55.810 --> 01:13:56.810
Immediately.

154
01:13:56.810 --> 01:13:58.810
They almost threw it to us.

155
01:13:58.810 --> 01:14:00.810
Simply amazing.

156
01:14:00.810 --> 01:14:03.810
And then came the financial year 2025,

157
01:14:03.810 --> 01:14:05.810
then Bram came into play,

158
01:14:05.810 --> 01:14:07.810
and Bram thought he was retiring,

159
01:14:07.810 --> 01:14:09.810
that he would finally have some peace there.

160
01:14:09.810 --> 01:14:16.810
And then Bram ended up working all year on finances,

161
01:14:16.810 --> 01:14:19.810
to a financial plan, to a forecast,

162
01:14:19.810 --> 01:14:23.810
to get the financing plan completely in order.

163
01:14:23.810 --> 01:14:25.810
And the financial advisors,

164
01:14:25.810 --> 01:14:28.810
the accounting firm we are going to in Geldermalsen,

165
01:14:28.810 --> 01:14:31.810
they said several times, this is perfect.

166
01:14:31.810 --> 01:14:33.810
Open Church is really doing its best.

167
01:14:33.810 --> 01:14:36.810
Dear people, when you come to Open Church,

168
01:14:36.810 --> 01:14:38.810
here is a church that is not perfect,

169
01:14:38.810 --> 01:14:40.810
it is filled with people and with you,

170
01:14:40.810 --> 01:14:42.810
so we will never become perfect,

171
01:14:42.810 --> 01:14:44.810
but we at least do our best. Amen?

172
01:14:44.810 --> 01:14:47.810
And we do our best to do things right.

173
01:14:47.810 --> 01:14:50.810
We do our best to give worship authentically to the Lord.

174
01:14:50.810 --> 01:14:52.810
Not for you, but for Him.

175
01:14:52.810 --> 01:14:56.810
We do our best to teach the Word of God as honestly as possible.

176
01:14:56.810 --> 01:14:57.810
We do our best.

177
01:14:57.810 --> 01:14:59.810
Do we ever miss the mark?

178
01:14:59.810 --> 01:15:00.810
I don't know.

179
01:15:00.810 --> 01:15:05.810
But Lord, help us to preach the Word of God in 2026 honestly and boldly

180
01:15:05.810 --> 01:15:07.810
and without fear,

181
01:15:07.810 --> 01:15:10.810
so that people can grow in the name of Jesus.

182
01:15:10.810 --> 01:15:11.810
We do our best.

183
01:15:11.810 --> 01:15:14.810
We do our best to handle every tenth

184
01:15:14.810 --> 01:15:18.810
and every sacrifice and every offering that you have given

185
01:15:18.810 --> 01:15:19.810
over the past years.

186
01:15:19.810 --> 01:15:24.810
Every euro is important and no euro is taken for granted.

187
01:15:24.810 --> 01:15:27.810
We think carefully about everything, about our administration,

188
01:15:27.810 --> 01:15:29.810
about how we handle the money,

189
01:15:29.810 --> 01:15:32.810
our long-term path, our vision for it,

190
01:15:33.810 --> 01:15:37.810
and when the financial advisors, the accountants in Geldermalsen,

191
01:15:37.810 --> 01:15:40.810
when they say, guys, you are doing it perfectly,

192
01:15:40.810 --> 01:15:43.810
then for me it is just thank you, Lord.

193
01:15:43.810 --> 01:15:46.810
Thank you, Lord, that we may do our best

194
01:15:46.810 --> 01:15:48.810
and that the Lord gives it growth.

195
01:15:48.810 --> 01:15:51.810
And I want to praise the Lord for the growth of Opelkerk.

196
01:15:51.810 --> 01:15:53.810
Glory to the Lord.

197
01:15:53.810 --> 01:15:58.810
And so in 2025 Bram is working on the financial plan,

198
01:15:58.810 --> 01:16:01.810
because we know we need to start building.

199
01:16:01.810 --> 01:16:04.810
We have the drawings, we have the permits,

200
01:16:04.810 --> 01:16:07.810
everything is a go, everything is on green light.

201
01:16:07.810 --> 01:16:09.810
and it actually went so easily

202
01:16:09.810 --> 01:16:12.810
that you can basically walk in in 2025

203
01:16:12.810 --> 01:16:14.810
and you think, well, that's coming easily.

204
01:16:14.810 --> 01:16:15.810
Haha, you know?

205
01:16:15.810 --> 01:16:19.810
I can imagine those first steps of Moses and the people of God,

206
01:16:19.810 --> 01:16:20.810
walking out of Egypt,

207
01:16:20.810 --> 01:16:23.810
I can imagine those first steps into the desert,

208
01:16:23.810 --> 01:16:27.810
but then suddenly you stand before a sea with a whole people.

209
01:16:27.810 --> 01:16:31.810
And that's how it felt for me a bit in the past few weeks.

210
01:16:31.810 --> 01:16:34.810
Because at a certain point, we all have the green light,

211
01:16:34.810 --> 01:16:37.810
pieces of land, permits, everything is go, go, go.

212
01:16:37.810 --> 01:16:38.810
Everything is going well.

213
01:16:38.810 --> 01:16:42.810
And then in 2025 you go to a number of banks

214
01:16:42.810 --> 01:16:43.810
and you say to the banks,

215
01:16:43.810 --> 01:16:45.810
hey, banks, can we have financing from you?

216
01:16:45.810 --> 01:16:46.810
Everything is in order.

217
01:16:46.810 --> 01:16:48.810
And all those banks that have helped us say,

218
01:16:48.810 --> 01:16:51.810
well, indeed, it really looks good.

219
01:16:51.810 --> 01:16:52.810
You are really doing well.

220
01:16:52.810 --> 01:16:55.810
This is good, but we are not going to do it.

221
01:16:55.810 --> 01:16:56.810
What?

222
01:16:56.810 --> 01:16:57.810
Yes, it looks good,

223
01:16:57.810 --> 01:16:58.810
but yes, you are a church.

224
01:16:58.810 --> 01:16:59.810
A church is strange.

225
01:16:59.810 --> 01:17:00.810
What is a church?

226
01:17:00.810 --> 01:17:01.810
What is a growing church?

227
01:17:01.810 --> 01:17:02.810
Why a growing church?

228
01:17:02.810 --> 01:17:03.810
No, we are not going to do that.

229
01:17:03.810 --> 01:17:06.810
Because banks are risk-averse.

230
01:17:06.810 --> 01:17:08.810
And another bank that said,

231
01:17:08.810 --> 01:17:09.810
no, no, no, we can't do that,

232
01:17:09.810 --> 01:17:11.810
because you have your property in Belgium,

233
01:17:11.810 --> 01:17:12.810
while we are a Dutch bank.

234
01:17:12.810 --> 01:17:13.810
We are not going to do that.

235
01:17:13.810 --> 01:17:15.810
And again a Belgian bank that said,

236
01:17:15.810 --> 01:17:16.810
yes, you are in Belgium,

237
01:17:16.810 --> 01:17:18.810
but your board is in the Netherlands,

238
01:17:18.810 --> 01:17:19.810
so the money must come from the Netherlands.

239
01:17:19.810 --> 01:17:20.810
We are not going to do that.

240
01:17:20.810 --> 01:17:23.810
And so ten banks had an answer every time.

241
01:17:23.810 --> 01:17:24.810
